  "question": {
    "text": "Three lines are given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and<br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#957;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#957;</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Let the lines cut the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at the points <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> respectively. If the area of the triangle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></math> then the value of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> equals_________"
  },
